 "keyHandling": "The API key was read from the environment or the git-ignored .env at build time. It is not in this file, the audio or the web build.",
 "timing": {
  "leadInMs": 350
 },
 "shots": {
  "what.alive": {
   "url": "01_what_alive.mp3",
   "bytes": 25536,
   "sha256": "e4399097092779973ef20b66b197fe98c04e460e93d4d16f60de43b243b9879b",
   "durationMs": 5960,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2130
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "This plant is alive. Like every living thing, it has to keep working just to stay alive."
  },
  "what.processes": {
   "url": "01_what_processes.mp3",
   "bytes": 27456,
   "sha256": "1da45eecdfbafe87c63b1de2f46d5b7c9aa65d7aed231d74af9976ee3cdbb6a8",
   "durationMs": 6560,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    3050
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "The jobs that keep it alive are called life processes. A plant makes its own food, and breaks food down to get energy."
  },
  "what.byproducts": {
   "url": "01_what_byproducts.mp3",
   "bytes": 25344,
   "sha256": "4f62179dc4e46b91abb3a544ebc329486f92c9e6723e3b45e1f70eb07b640b31",
   "durationMs": 6440,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    4270
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "But life processes also make substances the plant does not need. Some of them could even harm it if they stayed."
  },
  "what.excretion": {
   "url": "01_what_excretion.mp3",
   "bytes": 26976,
   "sha256": "9d6cad7dc2b231e581b1a3ca565eef39f7b57e70c03b9dcf33081d867fced6a7",
   "durationMs": 6200,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    3970
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Removing these harmful wastes from the body is called excretion. Every living thing has to do it in some way."
  },
  "what.question": {
   "url": "01_what_question.mp3",
   "bytes": 22176,
   "sha256": "baa9d63e6a4fcf894ad12f9994fdafbc996c732229e945600d787f31f09e5faa",
   "durationMs": 5480,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2960
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Plants also carry out life processes. So what happens to the substances they do not need?"
  },
  "different.animals": {
   "url": "02_different_animals.mp3",
   "bytes": 24192,
   "sha256": "74010761e040aa210ee3f1c0d6a7e668dfedaeb809f984b7ff8f597fd48a9f99",
   "durationMs": 6280,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    4000
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Many animals, like us, have special organs for this job. Our two kidneys filter wastes out of the blood."
  },
  "different.parts": {
   "url": "02_different_parts.mp3",
   "bytes": 20352,
   "sha256": "71ed956f3b6b9cfeef8a9a02c51f1bd03ac61e578391ae17470abe8fdc92f1bb",
   "durationMs": 5040,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    1500
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Now look at the plant. It has leaves, a stem with branches, and roots in the soil."
  },
  "different.none": {
   "url": "02_different_none.mp3",
   "bytes": 24576,
   "sha256": "051e4ce0ee8ef7eaca716ef5356e864480ae489a964cf8394ce3867f3df34f80",
   "durationMs": 6080,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2790
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "But none of these parts works like a kidney. Plants use completely different ways to deal with their wastes."
  },
  "different.question": {
   "url": "02_different_question.mp3",
   "bytes": 22464,
   "sha256": "daf86991779ef1e3eb7e06b1ae0070b16a88f4cdab72cf3135e1cd71775be35c",
   "durationMs": 7040,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2590
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "So here is our big question. If a plant has no special excretory organ, what does it do with its wastes?"
  },
  "different.plan": {
   "url": "02_different_plan.mp3",
   "bytes": 24384,
   "sha256": "bb654d08143c3df7138b06796e43852453cadd71218a7747146f3a379f901fe2",
   "durationMs": 6480,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    1700
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Let’s find out. We will follow the waste through the plant, one place at a time, starting high up at a leaf."
  },
  "oxygen.travel": {
   "url": "03a_oxygen_travel.mp3",
   "bytes": 11424,
   "sha256": "0d8e07a76205d2f9632059b4e90374c66581cfbe35671c6591e0889d56994874",
   "durationMs": 2800,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Our first stop is a leaf, high up on the plant."
  },
  "oxygen.look": {
   "url": "03a_oxygen_look.mp3",
   "bytes": 18912,
   "sha256": "0b7abc40907be8ebdf5189dd0699472088bc19a3fdf36beccec2d6e7bd052d59",
   "durationMs": 4680,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2020
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Leaves make the plant’s food. They do it by a process called photosynthesis."
  },
  "oxygen.photo": {
   "url": "03a_oxygen_photo.mp3",
   "bytes": 17856,
   "sha256": "c12bbdee2567663bd4b781a838b93de089b3cff08eeb56d22441f26a4a897bd7",
   "durationMs": 4400,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "In sunlight, the leaf uses carbon dioxide and water to make food."
  },
  "oxygen.produce": {
   "url": "03a_oxygen_produce.mp3",
   "bytes": 18336,
   "sha256": "0c5a89a1f56b8bc7c3e8897cd2c532eab5f9a539c5ed758772fbc5cd2e4bd4b6",
   "durationMs": 4920,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    3500
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Photosynthesis also makes a gas: oxygen. Watch it form in the leaf."
  },
  "oxygen.release": {
   "url": "03a_oxygen_release.mp3",
   "bytes": 15552,
   "sha256": "29b60822b20ffe183fc5d94a537f743ec997cb398e125a1a6b006e9e9d9755cc",
   "durationMs": 4200,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "The oxygen passes out of the leaf, into the air around the plant."
  },
  "oxygen.reason": {
   "url": "03a_oxygen_reason.mp3",
   "bytes": 37056,
   "sha256": "cc44e64c3cd347b0f1e793cef207edc28b7fd703ff04e1b467310015032a68bd",
   "durationMs": 10560,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    3700
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "The plant makes this oxygen and then gives it out. So oxygen can be thought of as a waste product of photosynthesis, and the plant gets rid of it by releasing it into the air."
  },
  "oxygen.try": {
   "url": "03a_oxygen_try.mp3",
   "bytes": 19776,
   "sha256": "2a27492375f1016bc05f883d1b0f06f87c23e142b2283c7a66b7adc42eb4a8ff",
   "durationMs": 4520,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    1220
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Your turn. Bring the sunlight to the leaf, and watch what comes out of it."
  },
  "water.question": {
   "url": "03b_water_question.mp3",
   "bytes": 24672,
   "sha256": "95d1e0bf260423ad01caceb0bc388a14478b71cfd16c98026670e1d943c0511f",
   "durationMs": 5960,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    4220
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "A plant also takes in a lot of water, often more than it needs. What happens to the extra water?"
  },
  "water.enter": {
   "url": "03b_water_enter.mp3",
   "bytes": 14496,
   "sha256": "05cad16243a65122069543985c7405e54b8bc9e1f6542b2042a5763fa0513408",
   "durationMs": 3000,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Water from the soil enters the plant through its roots."
  },
  "water.rise": {
   "url": "03b_water_rise.mp3",
   "bytes": 21312,
   "sha256": "e3869008404380f58689738afcedc292758e0b84644d7a4eb6608d33e93dfa17",
   "durationMs": 4800,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "It moves up the stem inside tubes called xylem, and out along the branches to the leaves."
  },
  "water.vapour": {
   "url": "03b_water_vapour.mp3",
   "bytes": 19776,
   "sha256": "c33573b6437a006d82ad0fafc14796bd96aab2358c79a76c946aebe4e5feb74a",
   "durationMs": 4920,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "In the leaves, some of this water turns into water vapour and escapes into the air."
  },
  "water.reason": {
   "url": "03b_water_reason.mp3",
   "bytes": 30144,
   "sha256": "abb546f3906a8a2a8ab69a13eff1d478254db0d6f225b1b61907b3e51abe3db2",
   "durationMs": 6960,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    4220
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Losing water as vapour like this is called transpiration. It is how a plant gets rid of its excess water."
  },
  "vacuole.pivot": {
   "url": "03c_vacuole_pivot.mp3",
   "bytes": 27744,
   "sha256": "826238ebd1878f0699418e2e46dd4994688b7e3cb645ac5107486b3eb3425d94",
   "durationMs": 6880,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    3210,
    5260
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Oxygen and extra water leave the plant. But some wastes are not removed at all. They are kept inside the plant."
  },
  "vacuole.dive": {
   "url": "03c_vacuole_dive.mp3",
   "bytes": 13632,
   "sha256": "46757398ed0a344d5875fffdeb7a11771478e403f99fbc6ada3eed8b1042422f",
   "durationMs": 3720,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "To see where, we need to zoom right into a leaf."
  },
  "vacuole.tissue": {
   "url": "03c_vacuole_tissue.mp3",
   "bytes": 17952,
   "sha256": "78d104c9079d55eb30dc58e7428eb10154083a5ffd970b283a539ea605ba9c9b",
   "durationMs": 4040,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Up close, a leaf is made of many tiny cells, packed together."
  },
  "vacuole.cell": {
   "url": "03c_vacuole_cell.mp3",
   "bytes": 33696,
   "sha256": "4ae2b000a8c5f78fc7846618df79ca0baafab9cd0dcbead5c482aacd5f8cc7a3",
   "durationMs": 7320,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2430
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Here is one of those cells, opened up. It has a cell wall, jelly-like cytoplasm, a nucleus, and one large vacuole."
  },
  "vacuole.store": {
   "url": "03c_vacuole_store.mp3",
   "bytes": 21792,
   "sha256": "52b89257a6c126b1baa63d24a377ec824e0fc611838e5fb521ab159a797cef30",
   "durationMs": 5400,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2930
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Now watch the wastes in the cytoplasm. They move into the vacuole, and there they stay."
  },
  "vacuole.reason": {
   "url": "03c_vacuole_reason.mp3",
   "bytes": 35712,
   "sha256": "d369d9578445fb89efc3839afadcc258eaf26dc3b49f3198dda3f4e309c1e330",
   "durationMs": 8880,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    3040,
    6470
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "The vacuole is a storage space inside the cell. Many plant waste products are stored in vacuoles like this one. They are kept, not removed from the plant."
  },
  "vacuole.try": {
   "url": "03c_vacuole_try.mp3",
   "bytes": 21984,
   "sha256": "5335967f80f425c1c6a5ffff76eb0d07e74e0a2e30d139bc78a87d48491d7ca5",
   "durationMs": 5440,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    1670,
    4030
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Your turn. A few wastes are still in the cytoplasm. Move them into the vacuole."
  },
  "vacuole.back": {
   "url": "03c_vacuole_back.mp3",
   "bytes": 17376,
   "sha256": "b91cb6661ac27d2b7d83a291784a8e6cd177ea953b59c132d9cc74cf8745f472",
   "durationMs": 4280,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Now let’s pull back out: from the vacuole, to the cell, to the leaf."
  },
  "vacuole.plant": {
   "url": "03c_vacuole_plant.mp3",
   "bytes": 19296,
   "sha256": "61dbf3979f1e1e5f40c157676c730ca1d8ecae979785afdaf90f0fa93479b30c",
   "durationMs": 5360,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2330
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "And back to the whole plant. Its leaves are made of cells like the one we just saw."
  },
  "leaves.lose": {
   "url": "03d_leaves_lose.mp3",
   "bytes": 20736,
   "sha256": "f726aef8ec7c4296c1147cf21e65197922e451d0e89b61769530337c32ba3b06",
   "durationMs": 5120,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2310
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Plants have another useful ability. They can even lose some of their parts, such as leaves."
  },
  "leaves.look": {
   "url": "03d_leaves_look.mp3",
   "bytes": 18336,
   "sha256": "8ead2a9679fb493524c321accb3cc7618269332932a970879395ee4a49b0b0a9",
   "durationMs": 5240,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    3050
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Look at this leaf, low down on the stem. It is one of the plant’s older leaves."
  },
  "leaves.load": {
   "url": "03d_leaves_load.mp3",
   "bytes": 24864,
   "sha256": "14e0ee7d08fe6ab661e5c7a1ecc00d7e795db1f895cebf874c0de6ad0b242abf",
   "durationMs": 5840,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    3390
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Some waste products are stored in leaves like this one. Time passes, and the leaf grows older."
  },
  "leaves.fall": {
   "url": "03d_leaves_fall.mp3",
   "bytes": 9696,
   "sha256": "6352967b49ee58ba51acbb4a8a5b75636403d450199ca6f443940cc64dde758b",
   "durationMs": 2320,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Then the leaf drops off the plant."
  },
  "leaves.reason": {
   "url": "03d_leaves_reason.mp3",
   "bytes": 33504,
   "sha256": "edb4550fe60b3e54af2c8924031b159cf6d6f8da375805fcbc7fadf8212f332a",
   "durationMs": 8880,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    4270
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "When the leaf falls, the wastes stored in it leave the plant too. Leaves also fall for other reasons, but this is one way a plant gets rid of wastes."
  },
  "resin.travel": {
   "url": "03e_resin_travel.mp3",
   "bytes": 20832,
   "sha256": "b6a699b5f5903c38b79d8ba4624bb57cb2cbc59d4ae9cbbcb9ebf7108124cef3",
   "durationMs": 5080,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2330
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Next, the stem. It looks solid from the outside, so let’s look inside it."
  },
  "resin.cut": {
   "url": "03e_resin_cut.mp3",
   "bytes": 23712,
   "sha256": "789414db0db41e46a60f79f8f258c12ecf2360a6d0f0869fae0cf674b2169856",
   "durationMs": 6160,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    3450
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Here is a magnified piece of the stem. As the top lifts away, we can see its layers."
  },
  "resin.layers": {
   "url": "03e_resin_layers.mp3",
   "bytes": 31104,
   "sha256": "303c6960dcd145ecac8b24ef092c354befcbfac36fa458cbce6fc59dd2449719",
   "durationMs": 8080,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2010
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Bark covers the outside. Inside are phloem, which carries food, and xylem, the same kind of tubes that carried water up the stem."
  },
  "resin.old": {
   "url": "03e_resin_old.mp3",
   "bytes": 24096,
   "sha256": "cfc65b0550f934f073090b8423c10021e7b26fcb7f398ebb4b106dd2332fa948",
   "durationMs": 6040,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    2680
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "This darker part is old xylem. Like many plant tissues, it is made mostly of dead cells."
  },
  "resin.store": {
   "url": "03e_resin_store.mp3",
   "bytes": 17664,
   "sha256": "5108b87767ac1ad15dcc6568c8c897dce9ee61ceffdbfa78c54c4f1b8cee9ce3",
   "durationMs": 4560,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    1300
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Watch. Some waste products are stored here, as resins and gums."
  },
  "resin.reason": {
   "url": "03e_resin_reason.mp3",
   "bytes": 30336,
   "sha256": "8f34b6e888055cc67393a0fadca16510118abfbe6a11a49dcaa61213a4f7115e",
   "durationMs": 6400,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    4090
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "So other waste products are stored as resins and gums, especially in old xylem. They are kept inside the stem, not removed."
  },
  "resin.try": {
   "url": "03e_resin_try.mp3",
   "bytes": 18624,
   "sha256": "08e97632520bd11431f1a4493472ef0d57e7478ebed4bd5896d5f47a4af61ab2",
   "durationMs": 4760,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
    1720
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Your turn. Find the part of the stem where resins and gums are stored."
  },
  "soil.travel": {
   "url": "03f_soil_travel.mp3",
   "bytes": 14976,
   "sha256": "d826e393bdd8d0ebca212df8249dd521e6f2f821f5a5a78f339a697d095ae485",
   "durationMs": 3760,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Our last stop is below the ground, around the roots."
  },
  "soil.look": {
   "url": "03f_soil_look.mp3",
   "bytes": 18336,
   "sha256": "15e9fec4f4b83ab4a200056fea980872f1648eea9dc07b46e720866c3b6fff7a",
   "durationMs": 4120,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0
   ],
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "The roots spread out through the soil, and the soil surrounds them on every side."
  },
  "soil.excrete": {
   "url": "03f_soil_excrete.mp3",
   "bytes": 22464,
   "sha256": "f834f8eb616be530e1083e8855f1c790596ce03e760a97b90e601552d1b3344c",
   "durationMs": 5400,
   "leadInMs": 350,
   "sentenceStartsMs": [
    0,
