  "recall.store.reveal": {
   "url": "cue_recall_store_reveal.mp3",
   "bytes": 16992,
   "sha256": "40f5d92a9f20443d9a998ab7c1a5a351756091b251c0024b346ce13226e9aabe",
   "durationMs": 5040,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Yes, that’s right. Many plant waste products are stored in cellular vacuoles."
  },
  "recall.leaves.question": {
   "url": "cue_recall_leaves_question.mp3",
   "bytes": 11136,
   "sha256": "cf2f31c44545d8bbe8b1d8e0d868b13f5e55be3fd86fa1d71213ef22efc75c65",
   "durationMs": 2880,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "What happens to leaves containing stored waste?"
  },
  "recall.leaves.reveal": {
   "url": "cue_recall_leaves_reveal.mp3",
   "bytes": 21792,
   "sha256": "b15e170b9e3cc571245ddd4d171fa5e9a22b27112999f3db2ce92998dce07f64",
   "durationMs": 6240,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Yes, that’s right. Wastes may be stored in leaves that later fall off, taking the wastes with them."
  },
  "recall.resin.question": {
   "url": "cue_recall_resin_question.mp3",
   "bytes": 11904,
   "sha256": "1d14e728c355ff6e9a3146e925cb46c84e776cd4d1030aec4f17b6af9d3b6ea1",
   "durationMs": 2800,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Where are resins and gums stored, especially?"
  },
  "recall.resin.reveal": {
   "url": "cue_recall_resin_reveal.mp3",
   "bytes": 16704,
   "sha256": "0b5ba1e2d2e3c29f31f6345932137a85d44afd78609f13f8ce25c66b859df355",
   "durationMs": 4360,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Yes, that’s right. Resins and gums are stored especially in old xylem."
  },
  "recall.soil.question": {
   "url": "cue_recall_soil_question.mp3",
   "bytes": 11136,
   "sha256": "d8ae8aae3cd84623b3000bc302e33a9ce047b7cc55ec19db0aeaf334e4cda971",
   "durationMs": 3040,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Where can plants excrete some waste substances?"
  },
  "recall.soil.reveal": {
   "url": "cue_recall_soil_reveal.mp3",
   "bytes": 22944,
   "sha256": "e9e26f87d2c36007dacd320153db27ff51c40b8283a591c5bca021a0070b31e1",
   "durationMs": 4720,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Yes, that’s right. Plants excrete some waste substances into the soil around them."
  },
  "recall.incorrect": {
   "url": "cue_recall_incorrect.mp3",
   "bytes": 11136,
   "sha256": "13c97fc4060f8dcce78649d10c2c9314252fafe1f6e9222e7d90b06e7d291d3a",
   "durationMs": 2920,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Not that one. Think back to what you saw."
  },
  "recall.open.prompt": {
   "url": "cue_recall_open_prompt.mp3",
   "bytes": 15552,
   "sha256": "d76118e15f38a23d50f4356fbba316c1e47db6d759f372d1fa2d715c5f321d1c",
   "durationMs": 3880,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Can you explain, in your own words, how plants deal with wastes?"
  },
  "recall.open.model": {
   "url": "cue_recall_open_model.mp3",
   "bytes": 73824,
   "sha256": "b3af383e601e5c0ae0df92d4f3b5bbce999f24350f93e029975851e57129a7a5",
   "durationMs": 18800,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Plants have no single excretory organ. Oxygen made in photosynthesis is released into the air, and excess water is lost as vapour by transpiration. Many wastes are stored in cell vacuoles, some in leaves that later fall off, and others as resins and gums, especially in old xylem. Some waste substances go into the soil."
  },
  "recall.complete": {
   "url": "cue_recall_complete.mp3",
   "bytes": 17952,
   "sha256": "ad7590ccd902c456dc4285093b8f69499519f52d9d9610516cc821775ed02f02",
   "durationMs": 3840,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Well done. You have followed the waste all the way through the plant."
  },
  "explore.intro": {
   "url": "cue_explore_intro.mp3",
   "bytes": 19392,
   "sha256": "19045b7eb3b3efc3591c25f89eedca2d01deafe6dc7e397f00a2c6fadf6d8b66",
   "durationMs": 5560,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Explore what you have learned so far. Turn a model, and tap a part to see what it is."
  },
  "explore.plant": {
   "url": "cue_explore_plant.mp3",
   "bytes": 26016,
   "sha256": "b3e1cfd2ad1ac0e1d02a596cc8fcf6ef6ac0afd2a2d0df5dfcd475d4baf07872",
   "durationMs": 6440,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "A plant has leaves, a stem with branches, and roots in the soil. None of these parts works like a kidney."
  },
  "explore.leaf": {
   "url": "cue_explore_leaf.mp3",
   "bytes": 26976,
   "sha256": "8fe41eefa1a385b421d8eb6ad526ac491b0ab6f3b5d89b07afde3877d70c3223",
   "durationMs": 6680,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Oxygen made in photosynthesis leaves the leaf into the air. Excess water leaves it as water vapour: transpiration."
  },
  "explore.cell": {
   "url": "cue_explore_cell.mp3",
   "bytes": 35232,
   "sha256": "56a386199c13f747e2a3ee8e6020b56c77f17bcb3b69cf3dd22a3729828b7496",
   "durationMs": 8080,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "A leaf is made of many cells. Each of these cells has a cell wall, cytoplasm, a nucleus and one large vacuole."
  },
  "explore.vacuole": {
   "url": "cue_explore_vacuole.mp3",
   "bytes": 24384,
   "sha256": "9120f6dcedf13fd4d08928713779fba2db84f34324281026f6690f0fd4a408ec",
   "durationMs": 5560,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Many plant waste products are stored in the vacuole. They are kept inside the cell, not removed."
  },
  "explore.stem": {
   "url": "cue_explore_stem.mp3",
   "bytes": 28416,
   "sha256": "d980bdd3d147d9630ee9f1de22cd31f0588ce16658d64f6fe760f0e78b762bdc",
   "durationMs": 7520,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "A magnified piece of stem: bark on the outside; inside it, phloem, which carries food, and xylem, which carries water."
  },
  "explore.oldxylem": {
   "url": "cue_explore_oldxylem.mp3",
   "bytes": 22176,
   "sha256": "8c88ee3ab7233b25008ef0985ec56a21f0bf243d6add170f28111c352f585901",
   "durationMs": 5120,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Old xylem is made mostly of dead cells. Resins and gums are stored especially here."
  },
  "explore.roots": {
   "url": "cue_explore_roots.mp3",
   "bytes": 17664,
   "sha256": "c258fb1b1c4ec1e99bc9933fb44811bf71b65f66935b1ad5f1ecb40dd83c492b",
   "durationMs": 4160,
   "leadInMs": 0,
   "voice": "en-IN-Chirp3-HD-Aoede",
   "speakingRate": 1,
   "text": "Some waste substances pass from the plant into the soil around its roots."
